<BaseLayout title="About & contact" description="Kangfeng (Randall) Ye: formal methods engineer, former York researcher, career background and contact links.">
  <div class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Research & engineering</p><h1>About Randall</h1><p>I am Kangfeng Ye, also known as Randall Ye. My work brings mathematical reasoning to the design and verification of software systems.</p></div>
  <div class="prose"><h2>Background</h2><p>Since November 2025, I have been a formal methods engineer at <a href="https://iohk.io/">IOHK</a>. Before this, I worked in research at the University of York on formal methods in robotics, probabilistic programming and security.</p><p>I completed my PhD at York between 2012 and 2016, supervised by Prof. Jim Woodcock. My thesis investigates model checking of state-rich formalisms by linking state-based specifications and process algebra.</p><p>From 2004 to 2012, I worked as an embedded software engineer and team lead on lithography, Ethernet datacentre switches and communications devices, using C/C++, microcontrollers, Linux and VxWorks.</p><ul class="inline-list"><li><a href={local('CV/Academic_CV-Kangfeng_Ye.pdf')}>Academic CV (PDF)</a></li><li><a href="https://etheses.whiterose.ac.uk/15526/">PhD thesis</a></li></ul><h2>Research collaborations</h2><p>Past projects include CHEDDAR (2024–2025), SESAME (2023–2024), RoboCalc and RoboTest (2018–2023), CyPhyAssure (2021), control-law diagram reasoning (2017–2018), and INTO-CPS (2016–2017).</p><p>I develop probabilistic verification support for RoboTool and have made selected contributions to Isabelle/UTP. My original homepage provides the detailed contribution notes and project links.</p><a href={local('legacy/#projects-i-was-or-am-working-on')}>Project history and academic activities →</a><h2 id="contact">Contact</h2><p>For personal contact: <a href="mailto:ye.randall@gmail.com">ye.randall@gmail.com</a>.</p><ul class="inline-list"><li><a href="https://github.com/RandallYe">GitHub</a></li><li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/randallye">LinkedIn</a></li><li><a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=PbLkCR8AAAAJ">Google Scholar</a></li><li><a href="https://dblp.org/pid/193/5774.html">DBLP</a></li></ul></div>
</BaseLayout>
